# truck-intel businesses rebuild (MASTER_PLAN §5.2: Overture/FSQ refresh monthly;
# ruling §3.1-6: the businesses derived job rebuilds core.businesses from staging).
#
# Chain semantics are deliberate (fail-safe rebuild):
#   1. --pull-overture   (NO leading '-'): the permissive primary source. If it
#      fails the service ABORTS before conflate, so a bad pull never rebuilds
#      core.businesses from empty/partial staging — the last good table stays live.
#   2. fsq_fetch.sh then --pull-fsq --fsq-local-dir (both leading '-'):
#      enrichment via the keyless source.coop mirror (no HF_TOKEN wait-item),
#      read from a LOCAL copy. Best-effort: a failure is ignored and conflate
#      proceeds Overture-only.
#      Local, not --fsq-mirror, since 2026-08-19: DuckDB's httpfs reader
#      against data.source.coop stalls — measured twice, a run reaches ~28-30 MB
#      then sits at 0-6 KB/s with sockets in CLOSE-WAIT and makes no progress
#      for the better part of an hour, while plain curl pulls from the same
#      host at 3.6 MB/s. fsq_places had NEVER succeeded until it was read
#      locally. fsq_fetch.sh re-verifies the mirror first (resumable, and a
#      no-op when nothing changed, since the release is frozen).
#   3. --conflate  (NO leading '-'): full rebuild + atomic snapshot swap, only
#      reached when the Overture pull succeeded.
# US-wide pulls are heavy (tens of GB of remote parquet scanned) — this is the
# monthly rebuild, not a tick job.
[Unit]
Description=truck-intel businesses rebuild (Overture + FSQ mirror -> conflate)
After=network-online.target docker.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/Documents/truck-intel
# per-pull runtime is long; systemd default has no timeout for oneshot, but be explicit
TimeoutStartSec=6h
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/uv run python scripts/businesses_pipeline.py --pull-overture
ExecStart=-%h/Documents/truck-intel/scripts/fsq_fetch.sh
ExecStart=-%h/.local/bin/uv run python scripts/businesses_pipeline.py --pull-fsq --fsq-local-dir data/fsq_places
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/uv run python scripts/businesses_pipeline.py --conflate

# Kernel ceilings, added 2026-07-27. `Nice`/`IOSchedulingClass` only lower
# PRIORITY — they never stop a job consuming the machine, which is what
# happened when an idle-classed OSM pass took the laptop from 11 GB free to
# 1.6 GB and had to be killed by hand. These bound a RUNAWAY; the admission
# gate in truckintel/resources.py is the first line of defence.
#
# These MUST sit inside [Service]. Appended after [Install] they parse as
# [Install] directives, systemd ignores them, and `systemctl show` reports
# MemoryMax=infinity while the unit file plainly reads MemoryMax=6G.
MemoryMax=6G
MemorySwapMax=0
CPUQuota=60%
